 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "Define the dot (scalar) product and list its properties.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Definition",
   "text": "\\( \\vec A\\cdot\\vec B = AB\\cos\\theta \\) (Eq 2.9) = (A cos θ) B = A (B cos θ): one magnitude times the component of the other along it. The result is a **scalar**. Examples: work, power, electric flux.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Properties 1–2",
   "text": "(1) **Commutative**: \\( \\vec A\\cdot\\vec B = \\vec B\\cdot\\vec A \\). (2) **Perpendicular** vectors give zero: \\( \\hat i\\cdot\\hat j = \\hat j\\cdot\\hat k = \\hat k\\cdot\\hat i = 0 \\); the dot product with a null vector is also 0.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Properties 3–4",
   "text": "(3) **Parallel** (θ = 0°): \\( \\vec A\\cdot\\vec B = AB \\) (maximum); \\( \\vec A\\cdot\\vec A = A^2 \\); \\( \\hat i\\cdot\\hat i = 1 \\). (4) **Anti-parallel** (θ = 180°): \\( -AB \\).",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Property 5: components",
   "text": "\\( \\vec A\\cdot\\vec B = A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z \\), so \\( \\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z}{AB} \\).",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Dot product",
   "tex": "\\vec A\\cdot\\vec B = AB\\cos\\theta = A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z",
   "text": "Eq 2.9, 2.13."
  }
 ],
 "challenges": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "type": "number",
   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "Find A · B for A = 2î + 3ĵ + k̂ and B = î − ĵ + 4k̂.",
   "answer": 3,
   "hint": "Multiply matching components and add.",
   "explain": "\\( 2(1) + 3(-1) + 1(4) = 3 \\).",
   "tolerance": 0.01
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "**A · B = AB cos θ** is a **scalar**.",
  "**Commutative**; 0 if perpendicular; **AB** if parallel; **−AB** if anti-parallel.",
  "**A · B = AxBx + AyBy + AzBz**."
 ]
